            <div xml:id="d337">

                <pb facs="0423" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4155: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-13T14:00:00+08:00">February 13, 1932—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 13—5:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. My telegram No. 37, February 12, 3 p.m. Notwithstanding assurance given
                    Admiral Taylor I am informed by telephone by Colonel Hooker that Japanese
                    bombing planes numbers 342 and 343 passed over American sector three times about
                    9 o’clock today.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation and Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
